WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.235
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Twenty.

2
00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:07.751
In any triangle, the sum of any two sides is greater than the remaining side.

3
00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:13.850
Given triangle A B C, we prove that any two of its sides taken together are greater than the third side.

4
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:21.760
Extend side B A to point D so that segment A D equals side A C, and construct segment D C.

5
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:28.265
Since A D equals A C in isosceles triangle A D C, base angle A D C equals angle A C D.

6
00:00:28.265 --> 00:00:35.836
Because the whole angle B C D is greater than its part A C D, angle B C D is also greater than angle A D C.

7
00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:43.195
In triangle D B C, the greater angle B C D is subtended by the greater side, so D B is greater than B C.

8
00:00:43.195 --> 00:00:54.940
Since D B is the sum of B A and A D, and A D equals A C, sides B A and A C together are greater than B C, and similarly for the other pairs, as was required to prove.
